  "notes": "\"The lane's most 90s-harmony-literate young tenor\", and the entry names his identifying parameter precisely: \"very dense multi-tracked 90s-style harmony (4–8 parts, **real voice-leading rather than parallel doubling**) — the stack arrangement is his identifying parameter — at moderate lead note-density\". Real voice-leading rather than doubling is why the counter is weighted onto `answer_lick` and `arp` instead of `octave_echo`, which is the setting the parallel-stack tenors in this section get, and why `topVoiceStepwise` is on with a high `adjacentSecondProb`. He produces and writes, so \"the harmony is chosen rather than looped\": 4-chord cycles that cadence, gospel passing chords, and a modulating final chorus. The kit is the lane standard with the roll vocabulary at 32nds rather than triplets, plus finger-snaps and a swung 90s kit on the retro cuts, which is `fullTimeVariantProb`. His form is stated as ending on \"a stripped a cappella-stack bridge\", which is the arrangement's high `dropOutBeats`. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**, mirroring medium-low: \"his producer-songwriter role is sourced; parametric detail is inference\". ⚠ All drum, swing and 808 numbers are **INFERRED**. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
